## Changes made

Renamed to "beautiful". Frontmatter reduced to `name` and `description` (the upstream
`license` key is dropped; licensing is recorded here and in LICENSE.txt instead), and the
description rewritten as triggering conditions only.

The hybrid takes the newer version's structure and voice as its spine, then restores the
material the rewrite dropped:

  - The tone menu of eleven named aesthetic directions, and the
    Purpose / Tone / Constraints / Differentiation questions (from 4ca561f)
  - Spatial composition — asymmetry, overlap, diagonal flow, grid-breaking (from 4ca561f;
    absent from d029127)
  - Backgrounds and visual detail — gradient meshes, noise, grain, layered transparency,
    custom cursors (from 4ca561f; absent from d029127)
  - Motion mechanics — CSS-only for plain HTML, the Motion library for React, staggered
    reveals via animation-delay (from 4ca561f), merged with the newer version's argument
    for using motion sparingly
  - Named anti-patterns — Arial/Inter/Roboto/system stacks, purple gradients on white,
    convergence on Space Grotesk (from 4ca561f), merged into the newer version's
    three-cluster calibration section
  - Explicit colour guidance and light/dark variation (from 4ca561f)
  - The closing "don't hold back" exhortation (from 4ca561f)

Retained in full from d029127: the studio framing, "ground it in the subject", hero-as-
thesis, "structure is information", the three-cluster calibration, the two-pass token-system
process with ASCII wireframes, the CSS specificity warning, the quality floor, the Chanel
restraint rule, and the entire "Writing in design" section.

One editorial reconciliation was necessary. The original urges committing to a BOLD
direction and not holding back; the rewrite urges spending boldness in one place and
removing one accessory before leaving the house. These are stated as a single position in
the hybrid, using the original's own formulation — "intentionality, not intensity" — as the
bridge: commit fully to a direction, then concentrate the boldness rather than spreading it.

No other substantive guidance from either revision was omitted.
